# patches/linux_mainline/series — quilt-style ordered apply list.
# One filename per line (relative to this dir). '#' = comment, blank lines OK.
# Applied by scripts/apply-series.sh via `git am` (run from the linux tree).
#
# RK3506 pinctrl+clk are already mainline; this series is the board/DT/driver
# delta on top of SoC support. Consolidated 2026-06-17 into 2 logical patches
# (DT + SFC driver) from explore/linux (base v7.1 = 8cd9520d3); reproduces the
# board-verified RW UBIFS rootfs (cold-reboot persistent, 3-cycle stress passed,
# PEB 3/4 page-recovered). Earlier 6-patch additive series squashed (it had a
# dead 80MHz patch immediately reversed to 50MHz + tuning split across patches).

# Board DT: rk3506.dtsi sfc node (compatible rk3506-fspi + grf phandle) +
# rk3506b-aes.dts (SFC enable + W25N04KV SPI-NAND + MTD partitions + 50MHz +
# max-dll + persistent-rootfs bootargs) + Makefile entry.
0001-ARM-dts-rockchip-rk3506b-aes-SFC-W25N04KV-SPI-NAND-R.patch
# SFC driver: DLL sampling tuning (vendor port) + SFC_CTRL_WPEN per op +
# per-transfer power-good gate (GRF_PMU+0x100 bit0). The RW-rootfs root-cause
# fix — makes Linux SFC reads/writes reliable (vendor fspi parity). Rootfs is
# then Linux-written by forge ubiprog so it survives cold reboots.
0002-spi-rockchip-sfc-DLL-tuning-RK3506-power-good-gate-W.patch

# DT 80MHz read speed (vendor EVB speed; +50% read, 100MHz unusable: 98MHz PLL tap no DLL window).
# Loader weak write on rootfs PEB3/4 covered by ubiprog first-boot rewrite.
0003-ARM-dts-rockchip-rk3506b-aes-bump-SFC-read-to-80MHz.patch
